<h1>Anna Schiefelbein</h1>
<p>Comptroller, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Green. Declared write-in.</p>
<p>These names are not printed on the ballot. To vote for one, write the name in the blank write-in space for that office and fill in the oval (on a touchscreen, follow the write-in steps on screen). Votes count only for write-ins who filed a declaration. The Chicago Board of Elections does not post those names, so this list comes from the Cook County Clerk&#39;s list and campaign announcements; election judges at your polling place have the official one.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Declared write-in candidate; the name is not printed on the ballot. She says she would end the state rule that drops companies from Illinois investments because they boycott, steer state investments toward relationships that protect air, water, and soil, and bring fiscal accountability after long one-party control.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Woodridge attorney with more than 20 years in accounting and finance who runs a small business; she was a write-in for Congress in Illinois&#39;s 11th District in 2024.</p>
